# <PROJECT_NAME> — shared agent context

> **This is the one home for shared project facts.** Claude Code reads it natively;
> Antigravity/Gemini reads it through `GEMINI.md`, a symlink to this file. Put anything
> both agents need here. A tool-specific `CLAUDE.md` or `GEMINI.md` should hold only that
> tool's own machinery or role — never a second copy of a fact from this file.
>
> Branches: Claude on `claude/<topic>`, Antigravity on `ag/<topic>`; neither on the
> default branch unless the owner asks.

Static HTML/CSS/JS, no runtime. Served from a domain root.

## Project

- **Site:** <SITE_URL>
- **Deploy target:** <DEPLOY_TARGET>

## Commands

```bash
npm run serve:export       # serve the build locally
npm test                   # Playwright suites
```

## Hard rules

- Internal links are root-absolute — the site **must** be served from a domain root.
- Never deploy a `STAGING=1` build to production (it carries noindex).
- Always `rsync --dry-run` before a real sync; `--delete` erases anything hand-placed.

## Operating rules

1. Verify after deploy: `PW_BASE_URL=<SITE_URL> npm test`
2. Get explicit sign-off before anything production-facing.

## Skills

Installed by Forge (`.claude/skills/`): static-export-build, playwright-verify,
deploy-static-cpanel, web-accessibility-wizard, ux-researcher,
design-motion-principles, context-budget, agent-interop.
